        "original_id": "71f19a55-9884-57d1-807c-c29e72f4d932",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John du Pont, Dave Schultz, Mark Schultz, Corey Jantzen\n- Works: Foxcatcher\n- Sports: freestyle wrestling, Team Foxcatcher\n\nFacts:\n- Dave Schultz was born on June 6, 1959.\n- In 1986, John du Pont recruited 1984 U.S. Olympic gold medalist brothers Mark Schultz and Dave Schultz to help coach U.S. wrestlers for national, world, and Olympic competition.\n- Foxcatcher is a film whose plot is loosely based on John du Pont’s recruitment of Mark Schultz and Dave Schultz and the later murder of Dave Schultz.\n- Dave Schultz was an American Olympic and world champion freestyle wrestler and a seven-time World and Olympic medalist.\n- On January 26, 1996, John du Pont murdered Dave Schultz.\n- Corey Jantzen worked on the Academy Award-nominated film Foxcatcher, where he played a wrestler on Team Foxcatcher and helped choreograph the wrestling sequences.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
